  "country": null,
  "description": {
    "de": "The government of Belarus decided to construct a nuclear power plant (NPP) with a capacity of 2,300–2,400 MWe. Austria takes part in the transboundary Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA) for the construction of the NPP in Belarus. The Environmental Agency Austria, “Umweltbundesamt” has assigned the Austrian Institute of Ecology, in cooperation with Dr. Helmut Hirsch, scientific consultant, to elaborate an expert statement on the EIA Report presented by Belarus."
  },
